    "id" : 27,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.662, 472.908, 525.542, 499.602 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Table 2: Results of analyzing the impact of individual feature groups in the ranking model when being used in isolation (on test set)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.607, 221.172, 292.176, 451.104 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "First, higher degrees of emotion in language use are clearly associated with category R proﬁles. Individual emotions most strongly associated with one of the categories are surprise, trust and disgust (for right-wing extremists), and love and sadness (for non-extremist users). Second, the most highly weighted pattern features for category R are GEGEN Masseneinwanderung (’mass immigration’), UNSER Politiker (’politicians’), UNSER Fahne (’banner’), GEGEN Syrien (’Syria’) and GEGEN Merkel, whereas UNSER Land (’country’), GEGEN Rechts (’Right-wing’), GEGEN Gebietsreform (’territorial reform’), PRO Aufkl¨arung (’information’) and UNSER Jugendkandidat*innen (’youth contestants’) are the most indicative patterns of category N."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 39,
    "level" : "Doctitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 193.505, 218.822, 209.059 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "5 Conclusions and Outlook"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 40,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 103.792, 290.651, 184.683 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In this paper, we have presented a ranking model to identify Twitter proﬁles which display traits or attitudes of right-wing extremism. Our work is motivated by the goal of supporting human experts in their monitoring activities which are currently carried out purely manually."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 41,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 75.859, 292.083, 102.553 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Similarly to standard nearest-neighbour classiﬁcation approaches, the model is based on estimat-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 42,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 306.763, 261.82, 527.458, 451.104 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "ing the relative proximity of an unseen proﬁle to a limited number of manually annotated groups of seed proﬁles in high-dimensional vector space. We apply this model in the two settings of discrete decoding and continuous ranking. Our evaluation shows a signiﬁcant advantage of the ranking model over a binary classiﬁcation approach (Hartung et al., 2017). At the same time, the ranking model is found to deliver plausible predictions for a sample of borderline cases which speciﬁcally address actors from New Right political movements in Germany, whose categorization as right-wing extremists is currently debated in the social sciences (cf. Zick et al., 2016)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 43,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 306.883, 89.408, 527.356, 238.045 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The latter ﬁnding clearly deserves a more thorough investigation based on a larger sample of cases, which we would like to address in future work. Additionally, we aim at developing this method further into a learning-to-rank approach in order to enable the comparison of proﬁles based on weighted properties. Finally, we propose the development of features that are based on deeper methods of natural language analysis in order to be able to address more ﬁne-grained aspects in the conceptualization of right-wing extremism."
  } ]
}